The requirement is "one HTTP callout per account" so the ERP can trace each record. That is honoured. However, a batch of 200 accounts would require 200 callouts in a single synchronous transaction, which exceeds the 100-callout governor limit. To keep the one-callout-per-account contract **and** survive the 200-record batch, I split the work into `@future(callout=true)` chunks of ≤ 100 accounts each. Each chunk runs in its own transaction (each gets its own fresh pool of 100 callouts). For the common 1-record path this is effectively one async callout—still triggered directly from the trigger, still one request per account.

---

